  "conclusion": "corresponds",
  "rationale": "Shared Eval/EvalArgs and local Step retain left-to-right atomic expression evaluation, destination freshness, struct guards and declaration-selected initial mode. Framed.Step wraps each local baseOperation in collection and has a separate empty-code frame exit. Steps/StepsExactly and Stuck supply finite executions and unfinished/no-successor. The equations use run and gc introduced in shared.machine/shared.gc. No intermediate expression collection or class sharing is introduced. The machine/gc/steps units introduce the lifetime notation; inherited syntax, storage and typing notation remain in the listed dependency units. Functions keeps its explicit inherited-machinery forward reference to the appendix.",
